we have 3nodes(green, blue, red)+2_other nodes with 3pods(green, blue, red) + 2_other nodes

ultimate aim is to place the blue pod in blue node and red pod in red node and green pod in green node
we are sharing kubernetes cluster with 2 other nodes, that needs to hold other pods

we dont want pods(green, blue, red) to be placed on other nodes
--------
solve using taints and tolerations:

we apply taints to nodes, by marking their color to (green, blue, red)

we set toleration on pods to tolerate the corresponding taint color

when pods are created, nodes ensuren that they only ensure to accept pods with the right toleration

However taints and toleration does not gaurantee that pods only prefer these nodes, so the pod can ends up on other nodes that do not have taints and tolerations set

this is not desired
--------

solve using node affinity and node selectors

we label nodes with their respective colors(green, blue, red)

we set node selectors on the pods to tie the pods to the nodes, so pods ends up on the right nodes

However, that doesn't guarantee that other pods are not placed on these nodes, there is a chance that other 2 pods can be placed on nodes having (green, blue, red) labels

this is not we desire
---------------------
 a combinatuion of taints&tolerations and node affinity rules can be used together to completely dedicate nodes for specific pods 

 we first use taints&tol to prevent other pods from being placed on our nodes
 the we use nopde affinity to prevent our pods from placing on other nodes



